---
import Section from "./Section.astro";

const points = [
  {
    title: "Your organization is the boundary",
    body: "Every request resolves your membership before it touches a row. Another organization's animal does not come back as forbidden; it comes back as not found, because as far as your session is concerned it does not exist. The database enforces the same rule underneath as a second net.",
  },
  {
    title: "Every change is attributable",
    body: "Mutations write an audit row - who, what, when, and the values before and after. Records are soft-deleted rather than erased, so something that was removed can still account for itself. Auditing is not a paid feature.",
  },
  {
    title: "Leaving is a supported operation",
    body: "CSV takeout of your animals and your logs is on every plan and carries no feature flag, and it keeps working after a trial lapses. Pro adds API tokens if you would rather pull it programmatically.",
  },
  {
    title: "Billing gates capture, never care",
    body: "The paywall is attached to creating new records. It is not attached to reading, searching, printing or exporting the ones you already have, and it never will be - a rescue that cannot pay this month still has to be able to look up what an animal was treated with last week.",
  },
  {
    title: "Photos and records back up together",
    body: "An image without its record is unreachable and a record without its image is a broken page, so the files and the database are treated as one backup unit rather than two schedules that can drift apart.",
  },
  {
    title: "No advertising, no data resale",
    body: "Your records are not a dataset that gets sold, aggregated for resale, or used to target advertising. The subscription is the business model.",
  },
];
---

<Section
  id="trust"
  tone="muted"
  eyebrow="Your data"
  title="It is your record. That has consequences for how ARK is built."
>
  <div class="mt-14 grid gap-x-10 gap-y-9 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
    {
      points.map((point) => (
        <div class="reveal">
          <h3 class="text-lg">{point.title}</h3>
          <p class="mt-2.5 text-muted-foreground">{point.body}</p>
        </div>
      ))
    }
  </div>
</Section>
